reading: stage 1 at T <= 256 (async / hybrid BM16-32, 1-2 waves per CTA) spends ~1.9-2.0k cycles per K step
  at 3-8% MFMA duty, the gaps being vmcnt waits on the weight stream (latency-bound, ST-1 / S1-D); at T >= 4096
  the pingpong runs ~1.5k cycles per step at ~34% duty per wave (2 waves per SIMD ~69%), gaps = the phase
  hand-off (s_setprio / s_nop). Stage 2 at small T is prologue / latency dominated (K = I is only 3-12 steps);
  at T=32768 the FC cells (I=768 / 1536) spend 47-64% of wave time in the fused-combine epilogue.
